[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Read by cause instead of by subject
line, its reports are three problems. The queued parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not known. Three problems, three tickets. The parser fix leaves two of them open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  repo="https://github.com/jasalguero/megadev_challenge"
  tickets={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day': 3 }}
/>

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads day-first dates month first.** This is the bug #4471
describes. It hits every day-first tenant, through the app, email and the `booking-v2` form. The
queued fix is for this one.

**`hint`: the `booking-v3` form tells day-first people to type month first.** The form prints
`MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says, and the form reads the date
the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not touch this path. The fix is the hint, for the
tenants that run `booking-v3`. Only reports sent through that form belong here.

**`one-day`: dates that move by one day, not by a month.** In these reports the day and month
are not swapped: a booking shows the day before, a client in Lisbon and a client in Toronto get
different days for one meeting, an invite arrives before its booking. That points at time zones,
not date order. The desk had already read these as a one-day move, then counted them under
`parser` by tenant.

## Why it was merged as one

- Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. All three problems
  produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite"), so subject matching puts them in one
  ticket. It cannot see the tenant's form or what the body says.
- `meta.intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the tenant both ways
  (see "tagged as"), so it cannot split the ticket either.
- The export repeats rows across its pages. Count by report id, not by row.

## For the desk

- Do not close #4471 as fixed when the parser fix ships: `hint` and `one-day` reports will keep
  coming.
- Triage date reports by tenant and channel (`causes.ts`), not by subject. A new decision record
  should replace 0001 for date reports.

